.Dd August 8, 2026
.Dt DOOR_UCRED 3C
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm door_ucred
.Nd return credential information associated with the client
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In door.h
.Ft int
.Fo door_ucred
.Fa "ucred_t **info"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn door_ucred
function returns credential information associated with the client, if any, of
the current door invocation.
.Pp
When successful,
.Fn door_ucred
writes a pointer to a user credential to the location pointed to by
.Fa info
if that location was previously
.Dv NULL .
If that location was non-null,
.Fn door_ucred
assumes that
.Fa info
points to a previously allocated
.Vt ucred_t
which is then reused.
The location pointed to by
.Fa info
can be used multiple times before being freed.
The value returned in
.Fa info
must be freed using
.Xr ucred_free 3C .
.Pp
The resulting user credential includes information about the effective user
and group ID, the real user and group ID, all privilege sets and the calling
PID.
.Pp
The credential information associated with the client refers to the
information from the immediate caller, not necessarily from the first thread
in a chain of door calls.
.Pp
For a door invocation made by the kernel on behalf of a process, the
credential reflects that process, with the exception of the calling PID, which
is reported as 0.
Since no user process can make a door call from PID 0, a door server which is
only intended to be called by the kernel can verify that by checking that
.Xr ucred_getpid 3C
returns 0.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Upon successful completion,
.Fn door_ucred
returns 0.
Otherwise, -1 is returned and
.Va errno
is set to indicate the error, in which case the memory location pointed to by
the
.Fa info
argument is unchanged.
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn door_ucred
function will fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EAGAIN
The location pointed to by
.Fa info
was
.Dv NULL
and allocating memory sufficient to hold a ucred failed.
.It Er EFAULT
The address of the
.Fa info
argument is invalid.
.It Er EINVAL
There is no associated door client.
.It Er ENOMEM
The location pointed to by
.Fa info
was
.Dv NULL
and allocating memory sufficient to hold a ucred failed.
.El
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
.Sy Committed
.Sh MT-LEVEL
.Sy MT-Safe
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr door_call 3C ,
.Xr door_create 3C ,
.Xr ucred_get 3C ,
.Xr attributes 7
